# Goal
Nothing I think about every day stays only in my head.

# Evals
- test: short enough to read in a minute → [ "$(intent words "$INTENT_FILE")" -le 250 ]
- judge: a stranger landing here can pick a post to read within 10 seconds
- review: it doesn't read like a template
- watch: something new ships at least once a week, here or anywhere else on the internet

# Fulfillment
I'm Mohamadreza, a software engineer building repeatable digital experiences for humans. Assistive AI has never been this good for me! I can finally share my thoughts about the things I never built to perfection.

This page is itself an .intent file: its goal is locked, and the evals check that the page still meets it. [Read it raw](/index.intent) or see [how the format works](/spec).

# Results
- judge 1: ✓ 2026-11-10 — two clearly titled posts under a Posts heading, visible without scrolling on desktop. On a phone the evals block pushes the list about 1.3 screens down, so it takes one scroll
